CAT = "phrebSaleMortgageLease"; SEG = "SML"
Q = [
("A sale of land made through an agent is void unless the agent's authority is:",
 "In writing", ["Notarized by the buyer", "Approved by the RD", "Given before witnesses"],
 "Article 1874 of the Civil Code: when a sale of land or any interest in it is through an agent, the authority of the agent must be in writing; otherwise the sale is void."),
("Under the Statute of Frauds, an oral agreement to sell a house and lot is:",
 "Unenforceable", ["Void from the start", "Valid and enforceable", "Rescissible"],
 "Article 1403 makes agreements for the sale of real property or an interest in it unenforceable by action unless in writing, though they are not void and may be ratified."),
("Earnest money given in a contract of sale of real property is:",
 "Part of the price and proof of perfection", ["A penalty forfeited whenever the buyer backs out", "A gift to the broker", "Returned after the sale"],
 "Article 1482 treats earnest money as part of the price and as proof of the perfection of the contract."),
("A buyer pays a separate sum to have 60 days to decide whether to buy a lot. That sum is the consideration for an:",
 "Option contract", ["Earnest money deposit", "Equitable mortgage", "Right of first refusal"],
 "An option is a separate contract giving the right to buy within a period. Under Article 1479 it binds the offeror only if supported by a consideration distinct from the price."),
("A seller sells the same lot to two buyers. Under Article 1544, ownership goes to the buyer who:",
 "First registers in good faith", ["Paid the higher price", "Signed the earlier contract only", "Lives nearer the lot"],
 "For immovables, ownership belongs to the buyer who first registers in good faith; if none registered, to the first possessor in good faith; failing that, to the one with the oldest title in good faith."),
("A contract to sell differs from a contract of sale because in a contract to sell the seller:",
 "Keeps title until full payment", ["Must deliver the title on the day of signing", "Cannot ask installments", "Pays the buyer's taxes"],
 "In a contract to sell, ownership stays with the seller and passes only when the buyer pays in full, a suspensive condition. In a contract of sale, ownership passes on delivery."),
("A clause letting the lender keep the mortgaged land automatically if the debtor fails to pay is:",
 "Void as pactum commissorium", ["Valid if notarized", "Valid when the lender is a bank or a lending firm", "Required by law"],
 "Article 2088 bars the creditor from appropriating or disposing of the mortgaged thing. Any contrary stipulation, pactum commissorium, is null and void; the creditor must foreclose."),
("Under the Civil Code, a real estate mortgage binds third persons only when it is:",
 "Recorded in the Registry of Property", ["Signed before two witnesses and the lender", "Approved by the barangay", "Paid in full"],
 "Article 2125 requires a mortgage to be recorded in the Registry for it to be validly constituted as a real right binding third persons. Unrecorded, it still binds the parties."),
("Maria 'sells' her lot with a right to repurchase but stays in possession and keeps paying the taxes. The law presumes the deal is:",
 "An equitable mortgage", ["An absolute sale", "A donation", "A lease"],
 "Article 1602 presumes an equitable mortgage when, among others, the vendor stays in possession or keeps paying taxes, so the 'buyer' must foreclose rather than consolidate title."),
("A tenant under a lease of a commercial space may assign the lease to another person only:",
 "With the lessor's consent", ["Whenever all the rent is paid up to date", "After six months", "With a broker present"],
 "Article 1649 bars the lessee from assigning the lease without the lessor's consent, unless the contract allows it."),
("A lease of real property for more than one year must be in writing to be:",
 "Enforceable", ["Valid at all", "Taxable", "Renewable"],
 "Under the Statute of Frauds (Article 1403), an agreement for leasing real property for longer than one year is unenforceable by action unless it is in writing."),
("A judicial action to evict a lessee for non-payment of rent is an action for:",
 "Unlawful detainer", ["Forcible entry", "Quieting of title", "Partition"],
 "When possession was lawful at first but became unlawful after the lease ended or rent went unpaid and a demand was made, the remedy is unlawful detainer under Rule 70."),
]
